Final verification: the mesh contains 9,216 all-hexahedral cells in one connected region; bare `checkMesh` reports `Mesh OK`, maximum non-orthogonality 0.96°, maximum skewness 0.130, and positive cell volumes throughout. The six STL patches in `constant/triSurface` are generated from the same refined boundary vertices as the volume mesh.

Built/measured against the request:
- neck outside diameter: 40.0 mm;
- single-start pitch: 2.0 mm;
- radial thread depth: 1.0 mm;
- helical advance: 12.0 mm = 6 turns;
- neck-to-lid flank clearance: 0.2 mm normal to the flank;
- separately named `neckFlank`, `lidFlank`, `innerEnd`, and `outerEnd`;
- additional closing wall patches: `threadRoot` and `threadCrest`.

Assumptions: a standard 30° included trapezoidal thread angle because no flank angle was specified; the 0.2 mm “shallower” cut was interpreted as a uniform normal flank clearance. The inclined flank and clearance make the full surface bounding-box height 12.461 mm although the requested helical advance is exactly 12 mm. No flow boundary conditions or solution setup were added.
